From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:08:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/intc/openpic: restore the CPUs' external proxy mode on
 load

On e500 the MPIC's external proxy mode (GCR mode bits = proxy) makes
the core acknowledge the MPIC when it delivers an external interrupt,
latching the vector in EPR. QEMU keeps that mode in each CPU's
env->mpic_proxy, which only openpic_gcr_write sets. gcr is migrated but
openpic_post_load never re-derives mpic_proxy, so after a load it is
false: external interrupts are delivered without the IACK, the line
stays asserted and EPR is stale.

Repro without record/replay: boot Linux on ppce500 (it selects proxy
mode), savevm, then -loadvm in a new process. The guest takes the same
external interrupt forever (NIP stuck at its handler) and makes no
progress. Under record/replay the replay diverged at the first external
interrupt after the start snapshot, which is why ppc32 rr never
finished.

Set the proxy mode from the loaded GCR in openpic_post_load, the same
call the GCR write makes. Snapshots are unchanged: one from an unfixed
build loads (and now runs) in a fixed one, and a guest that never chose
proxy mode gets false, as before. mac99, whose OpenPIC has no mode bits,
still saves and loads.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Origin: new
---
 hw/intc/openpic.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/intc/openpic.c b/hw/intc/openpic.c
index 99d2a1e65ec5868fa7fc7ebceca8debe45a14e60..6574c54b17fc6ab95e362295449f907201841793 100644
--- a/hw/intc/openpic.c
+++ b/hw/intc/openpic.c
@@ -1460,6 +1460,13 @@ static int openpic_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
         write_IRQreg_ivpr(opp, i, opp->src[i].ivpr);
     }
 
+    /*
+     * The CPUs' external proxy mode is set only by a GCR write: set it from
+     * the loaded GCR, or a restored guest that uses proxy mode gets external
+     * interrupts that are never acknowledged on delivery.
+     */
+    ppce500_set_mpic_proxy((opp->gcr & opp->mpic_mode_mask) == GCR_MODE_PROXY);
+
     return 0;
 }
 
